From 8a3bcbbbb3383d2eee67193ce3d5da390711422c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:23:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] bcm2835-sdiod: network interface wlan0 after the join,
 PMK from the passphrase

After a join the driver stays and registers network.wlan0, which netstack
takes as wlan0: Ethernet frames go out and come in on SDPCM channel 2
with a BCDC data header. It polls the SDIO core every 2 ms while idle
(no interrupt yet) and logs frame counters once a minute.

The firmware supplicant now gets the WPA2 PMK as 64 hex digits, as from
Linux' brcmfmac, computed here with PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1 (tested with the
IEEE 802.11 annex J vectors). /etc/net/wifi also takes ssid_hex= and
psk_hex=, for names and passphrases a shell would mangle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
